#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SE2276 expect=violation domain=MI
#note "Subject 001's latest disposition starts 2020-01-20. Row 1: collected 2020-01-05 (matches only the earlier, superseded disposition) -> offending. Row 2: collected 2020-01-22, after the disposition -> offending. Row 3: collected on the disposition date -> clean. O-4 (Fix #337, owner 2026-08-22 'the issue is by subject'): the rule carries Grouping: {Variables: [USUBJID]}, so the two offending rows of ONE subject fold into ONE finding, anchored at the subject's first flagged row (row 1). Re-pinned 2 -> 1; a per-record reading would report 2 here. Phase 5b (D58/D94b): MIDTC varies across the two flagged rows, so the finding renders the distinct set [2020-01-05, 2020-01-22] instead of the anchor row's arbitrary value."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 MIDTC="[2020-01-05, 2020-01-22]"
dataset MI label="Microscopic Findings"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col MISEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col MITESTCD type=Char label="Microscopic Examination Short Name"
col MISPEC   type=Char label="Specimen Material Type"
col MIORRES  type=Char label="Result or Finding in Original Units"
col MIDTC    type=Char label="Date/Time of Collection"
---
S1 | MI | 001 | 1 | MIEXAM | LIVER  | NECROSIS | 2020-01-05
S1 | MI | 001 | 2 | MIEXAM | KIDNEY | NORMAL   | 2020-01-22
S1 | MI | 001 | 3 | MIEXAM | SPLEEN | NORMAL   | 2020-01-20
---

dataset DS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSTERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Disposition Event"
col DSDECOD type=Char label="Standardized Disposition Term"
col DSSTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Disposition Event"
---
S1 | DS | 001 | 1 | MOVED TO RECOVERY  | RECOVERY           | 2020-01-05
S1 | DS | 001 | 2 | TERMINAL SACRIFICE | TERMINAL SACRIFICE | 2020-01-20
